  "question": {
    "text": "A superconducting loop of radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> has self-inductance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>. A uniform and constant magnetic field <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is applied perpendicular to the plane of the loop. Initially current in this loop is zero. The loop is rotated by <math><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. The current in the loop after the rotation is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "zero",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Initially, the current was zero, so self-induced flux was also zero. Now when we rotate the loop, the change in flux is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math><br /><br />Finally, to maintain the same zero flux, the current in the superconducting loop will be such that the flux due to induced current will negative of the flux due to external field<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
}